<title>USA: USTR negotiator Shapiro to leave administration.</title>
<headline>USTR negotiator Shapiro to leave administration.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senior U.S. trade negotiator Ira Shapiro is planning to leave the Clinton administration, officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>But the officials, who declined to be identified, said he will probably not depart for another few months.</p>
<p>As Senior Counsel and Negotiator at the U.S. Trade Representative's Office, Shapiro has been the key U.S. trade negotiator with Japan, Canada and Mexico.</p>
</text>
